## Performance Guidelines

### Memory Management
- Use generators for large data processing
- Implement proper cleanup in finally blocks
- Monitor memory usage in long-running processes
- Set DataFrame size limits (100MB default)
- Use connection pooling for databases

### Caching Strategy
- Cache expensive computations (anomaly detection, chart generation)
- Use Redis for distributed caching
- Implement cache invalidation strategies
- Cache API responses when appropriate

## Security Guidelines

### Input Validation
- Validate all user inputs using Pydantic models
- Sanitize file paths to prevent directory traversal
- Use parameterized SQL queries only
- Implement rate limiting on API endpoints
- Never log sensitive data (API keys, passwords)

### Session Management
```python
# Use Redis for session storage in production
# Implement session expiration (default: 1 hour)
# Generate secure session IDs
# Clear sensitive data from sessions on logout
```

## Development Workflow Commands

### Setup Commands
```bash
# Install development dependencies
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt

# Setup pre-commit hooks
pre-commit install

# Run all formatting and linting
pre-commit run --all-files

# Run tests with coverage
pytest --cov=ai --cov-report=html

# Type checking
mypy ai/
```

### Daily Development
```bash
# Auto-format code (runs on save in VS Code)
black ai/ tests/
isort ai/ tests/
autoflake --remove-all-unused-imports --in-place --recursive ai/ tests/

# Run specific test types
pytest -m unit
pytest -m integration
pytest -m "not slow"
```

## San Francisco Data Context

### Dataset Characteristics
- Large time series datasets (police incidents, 311 calls, permits)
- Geographic data with supervisor districts (0-11)
- Multiple data sources with different schemas
- Real-time and historical data
- Public datasets with privacy considerations

### Domain-Specific Patterns
- Always filter by supervisor district when relevant
- Handle date ranges properly (fiscal vs calendar years)
- Use appropriate aggregation methods for different metrics
- Consider seasonality in trend analysis
- Validate geographic boundaries

### Anomaly Detection Patterns
- Use statistical methods appropriate for the data type
- Consider external factors (holidays, events, weather)
- Provide explanations for detected anomalies
- Set appropriate thresholds for different metrics
- Track anomaly detection accuracy over time

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

❌ **Don't Do This:**
- Global variables for state management
- Monolithic files >500 lines
- Manual import management
- Unused imports or variables
- Missing type hints
- Hardcoded configuration values
- Blocking operations in async functions
- Unvalidated user input

✅ **Do This Instead:**
- Dependency injection for state
- Modular files with single responsibilities
- Auto-managed imports with pre-commit hooks
- Comprehensive type hints
- Environment-based configuration
- Async operations for I/O
- Pydantic validation for all inputs
- Automated code quality checks

Remember: This is a data analysis platform for civic transparency. Code should be reliable, well-documented, maintainable, and automatically formatted for long-term use.